{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1589f315b690b13265b2e92e0b57bae1bc305df92dc0668dd4d97ae6e326e6e3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_51ada53fcbc4f60df93f903de568f0292afe70c6cff9374f4e04d27a140955c7"],"source_ids":["src_83dceec3784052a09cea4752da3be4fa"],"text":"The product organizes work hierarchically: a machine is a runtime endpoint, a project is a folder on it, a workspace is a provider-owned working folder, and a session is a Pi Coding Agent chat inside a workspace.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8967c45b5d29a110cdac6308247608e5f58ccb0c57c0ee54df69052f026a0011","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1a3bd483bc6078988a166993eb8ae11c9d71ad2c8832f8e54fc462aacda107e5"],"source_ids":["src_83dceec3784052a09cea4752da3be4fa"],"text":"Running PI WEB requires Node.js 22.19.0 or newer, npm, a Pi Coding Agent of at least version 0.84.0, and git plus the development tools agents need.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a4d9cf321f8ecae1861ede17de1fd1a7e7553eb219d6e9ed4c289cf1f66d1714","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_09153479bf66385f87f79810ab0517cad2c93846b2036864a2e466b669c1d768","slc_5ce822156e5da02819a05ad07302d6c56f44b3d7cd96f5bfe614d5ce589de7c3"],"source_ids":["src_83dceec3784052a09cea4752da3be4fa"],"text":"Installation uses npm with the scoped --allow-scripts=node-pty flag so node-pty can build its native module without enabling install scripts for other packages.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d530a1f25c83e05f228999bdb8b54f6c8ade851927ab79df85ac03529400b050","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_20d14fccc8c0e7544d078deb63abecff954cb1f0321991225078550ff10f4cd7","slc_41551ebc61db749eea27c37678501df15e653e8fd82efd5403bc4b152aa53bdf"],"source_ids":["src_83dceec3784052a09cea4752da3be4fa"],"text":"The security model assumes trusted users, repositories, and server paths; the product is explicitly not a sandbox, permission system, or multi-tenant platform and should not be exposed directly to the public internet.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d60f58ee64c1335c77a3db2cdbda825769fcaafa33eba90b80c6f1faa15a259c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_609f25774f42885b122dd93999df4490c7aabfbec164fd0116b05fa08d18f6a6","slc_a888cfaf4545a5e50f1c03b4fee5a1c6371eca3920e6f449c994a6d787e77ca9"],"source_ids":["src_83dceec3784052a09cea4752da3be4fa"],"text":"Sessions are designed to survive browser disconnects, letting users supervise agents from any browser while work continues on the host machine.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d93387b1a99c554df0f156da90a3c302707cccbcc40c0346c3d9f69519e5bcde","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b9de41441998b515d7ccb616f8864106a7ae5e2072a7e7fba0d6bdf2cd9d5cd","slc_80bca31cd895d5d5892a8f41efd5682acfe52288d68bf897b225d87eaae3a42b"],"source_ids":["src_68bb307225295cee8b4ab485112cfe7f"],"text":"PI_WEB_DATA_DIR sets the root for managed runtime state (default ~/.pi-web), holding project and machine registries, discovered plugins, the session-daemon socket, and session archives; each data directory starts independent and empty.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e50a8246cedf5912f0eae6378494203698501ec6ef69568902a56b87cd1b1640","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a20fa5fd5cb96e76bcb4ea4bf723b3c136cb090710abd4db9266a71afad97c3d"],"source_ids":["src_68bb307225295cee8b4ab485112cfe7f"],"text":"One live session daemon owns each data directory, recording ownership in sessiond-owner.json; a second daemon pointed at the same directory fails loudly at startup, while stale markers from dead daemons are taken over automatically.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e59eb1dd41b81a120cdc28850402c76e612d4b7040b2482363470b04bb408920","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2ab1dc8b84498ab019812227c9925de60ebb1e3d1a35d528d479c798d807c188","slc_363296cd49b2d3f87054ebfb83f9a7f8123ee68be7adffb3109ea23fc3c48f43","slc_4b6d20605241668ad087378a5c84822d97e406426feb46465a2b9ff109963c32","slc_6cdee19e3fda51fa1fc99317e7c2d66ded733d203280032ad9b2dc65c37ea1f0"],"source_ids":["src_68bb307225295cee8b4ab485112cfe7f"],"text":"By default workspace-relative file reads stay inside the workspace and absolute paths are denied; pathAccess.allowedPaths grants the file explorer access to specific external filesystem roots, with symlink escapes rejected, though this is not a sandbox for the agent or OS user.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f998c5bb9928e7ded53452411afad097e2584eec3bed5c2d253048c983e6e9c6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_26c8c05923a2bce47e1a33b3f59e2f992af4f7dcdea1a384d0cf458f151740ef","slc_321115cbcacf4a980211adaa6a866cdef44087bfaebde02a6436aee453b6a24c","slc_65fd6b31158447b65bf0d61c925192c5d4f2b514b806adfbbee89ff2a7ed5dfa"],"source_ids":["src_68bb307225295cee8b4ab485112cfe7f"],"text":"Configuration resolves as defaults, then the global config file, then environment overrides; project-local <project>/.pi-web/config.json can override upload and attachment defaults and merge allowed paths.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fa44460aebcf86a4b35d21cf46d876604f4f4c08595a17520f18b6c93974cb11","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jmfederico/pi-web@46579c049a30 snapshot 3287e18d140e16b7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a29470d7ad0188adc37e3975f983bd081b59b4167677a3725da2cea5c3487042"],"source_ids":["src_83dceec3784052a09cea4752da3be4fa"],"text":"PI WEB can register other PI WEB runtimes as remote machines, with one browser-facing instance proxying projects, files, git state, sessions, terminals, and Pi package management from trusted remote machines.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_636c316dd368487894232d38f828d83f"}
